  The parallel split held: each agent staged only its own pathspec, so the two commits are disjoint and neither swept up
  the other's files. I kept [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m and [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m out of both agents' hands and edited them after collecting,
  which is why there was nothing to reconcile.

  Two behaviors the agents chose that you may want to overrule — both are pinned by tests, so changing them means
  changing a test:

  - [1m[38;5;153mslugify[39m is ASCII-only.[0m Anything that doesn't decompose to [38;5;153m[a-z0-9][39m under NFKD is treated as a separator, so a title
    written entirely in Cyrillic, CJK, or emoji slugifies to [38;5;153m''[39m. Transliteration would need a dependency; punting on it
    is the zero-dep answer, but it's a real limitation if titles can be non-Latin.
  - [1m[38;5;153mtruncate[39m counts UTF-16 code units, not grapheme clusters.[0m Slicing at [38;5;153mn - 1[39m can split a surrogate pair, leaving a
    lone surrogate before the ellipsis when the cut lands mid-emoji. The length bound still holds; the character may
    render as a replacement glyph.

  Also worth knowing: both treat boxed [38;5;153mnew String('x')[39m as non-string and return [38;5;153m''[39m, which follows the contract I gave
  them but is arguably surprising.

